{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["Heavy — Pharaoh makes his heart heavy, as I explained above, for verbs of bodily conditions one says וְיִשְׁמַן, וַיִּכְבַּד, וַיִּשְׁפַּל, וַיִּזְקַן, וַיֶּחְכַּל [sic], and from them one says in the past זָקֵן, כָּבֵד, שָׁמֵן, וְשָׁפֵל — all of them pa'al forms."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The lemma 'כבד' corresponds to the phrase 'כבד לב פרעה' in Exodus 7:14. The text reads 'ורום אנשים' which is literally 'and the height of men'; the sense and the reading are uncertain and rendered here hyper-literally. The form 'וַיֶּחְכַּל' appears corrupt; it may stand for וַיֶּחְכַּם ('and he became wise'), matching the preceding list."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:40.311893527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}